------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Composition: web `<VisuallyHidden as="a" focusable>` skip link -> native shared `TsButton` primitive,
  visually hidden until keyboard focus (opacity 0 -> 1 on GotFocus; -> 0 on LostFocus), revealed top-left.
- Data: web `useTranslation` -> ILocalizer facade (P1/S10). Single i18n key `translation.a11y.skipToContent`
  ("Skip to main content") — already present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw.
- Behaviour: web onClick `const main = getElementById('main-content'); if (main) { main.focus(...);
  main.scrollIntoView(...) }` -> ISkipTarget seam (P1/S8): ControlSkipTarget focuses + StartBringIntoView;
  NullSkipTarget is the no-landmark no-op (the web `if (main)` guard falling through — never throws).
- States reproduced (the web source has NO data fetch, so NO loading/empty/error/stale/offline chrome — same
  as the peer a11y surfaces RouteAnnouncer / VisuallyHidden): resting (hidden) link, focused (revealed) link,
  activation-with-landmark (focus moved), activation-without-landmark (safe no-op).
- Accessibility: link carries the localized accessible name + automation id "skip-to-content" (web
  data-testid); instant opacity reveal => reduce-motion-safe by construction; WinUI scales with system font size.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): emits `view.opened slug=SkipToContent` once on Loaded; also `skip.activated` /
  `skip.targetMissing` operational counters. PII-safe (slug-only; never the label or landmark text).

